Add your chipotle paste to a large bowl with a drizzle of olive oil, ground smoked paprika, ground coriander, half the lime zest (you''ll need the rest later!), garlic, your chicken and a generous pinch of salt and then give everything a good mix.

Finally, combine your chicken stock and tomato paste to create your tomato stock.', null),
  ('chipotle-chicken', 3, 'Heat a large, wide-based pan with a rather generous drizzle of olive oil over a high heat, and once hot, add your now marinated chicken strips with 1 tsp flour and cook until lightly browned on both sides.

Once browned, add the tomato stock to the pan and cook, covered, for 10-12 min further or until the chicken is cooked through (no pink meat!)', null),
  ('chipotle-chicken', 4, 'Whilst the chicken is cooking, add your carrot & cabbage slaw mix to a bowl with the juice of half the lime, your mayo and a pinch of salt and pepper. Give everything a good stir to create your home-made slaw!', null),
  ('chipotle-chicken', 5, 'Dice your tomatoes and cut the remaining zested lime into wedges. Add the diced tomato to a bowl with the left over lime zest, a dash of lime juice, a drizzle of olive oil and a pinch of salt and pepper to form your tomato lime salsa!', null),
  ('chipotle-chicken', 6, 'Time for the fun part - once coked, transfer the chicken onto a clean board and shred it apart, using two forks. Return your pulled chicken to the pan and give everything a good mix up so the chicken is evenly coated in the sauce. Serve atop the cooked rice, with your slaw and salsa to the side.', null),
  ('cottage-cheese-recovery-pot', 1, 'Spoon the cottage cheese into a bowl.', null),
  ('cottage-cheese-recovery-pot', 2, 'Stir the oats straight through it. They soften as they sit, so this is better made ten minutes before you eat it.', null),
  ('cottage-cheese-recovery-pot', 3, 'Add the blueberries and the honey.', null),
  ('cottage-cheese-recovery-pot', 4, 'Scatter the almonds over the top for something to bite on.', null),
  ('fruity-cous-cous', 1, 'In a heatproof dish, combine your couscous, sultanas and diced apricots.', null),
  ('fruity-cous-cous', 2, 'Boil a kettle and dissolve your vegetable stock cube in 250 ml of boiling water.', null),
  ('fruity-cous-cous', 3, 'Pour your stock over the couscous and fruit and give everything a good stir. Cover with a tea towel and set to one side, leaving it to soak up the stock for 5 to 10 minutes, stirring occasionally to make it fluffy.', null),
  ('fruity-cous-cous', 4, 'Dice your tomatoes and cut a lemon into wedges.', null),
  ('fruity-cous-cous', 5, 'Once the couscous has absorbed the stock, add a drizzle of olive oil, the juice of one lemon wedge and the chopped tomatoes. Stir, top with the flaked almonds and serve.', null),
  ('greek-yogurt-berry-bowl', 1, 'Spoon the yogurt into a bowl and level it off.', null),
  ('greek-yogurt-berry-bowl', 2, 'Pile the berries over one half and the granola over the other, so the granola stays crunchy for longer.', null),
  ('greek-yogurt-berry-bowl', 3, 'Drizzle over the honey and scatter the pumpkin seeds.', null),
  ('greek-yogurt-berry-bowl', 4, 'Eat straight away, or cover and take it with you.', null),
  ('honey-banana-toast', 1, 'Toast the bread.', null),
  ('honey-banana-toast', 2, 'Slice the banana over both slices.', null),
  ('honey-banana-toast', 3, 'Trickle the honey on and eat within the next few minutes, while the toast is still warm.', null),
  ('lemon-chicken-new-potatoes', 1, 'Heat the oven to 200C fan. Toss the potatoes with half the oil, the garlic and plenty of salt, and roast for 15 minutes.', null),
  ('lemon-chicken-new-potatoes', 2, 'Rub the chicken with the rest of the oil and season it well.', null),
  ('lemon-chicken-new-potatoes', 3, 'Push the potatoes to one side of the tray, add the chicken and the lemon slices, and roast for another 15 minutes.', null),
  ('lemon-chicken-new-potatoes', 4, 'Add the green beans to the tray and give everything a shake. Back in for 5 minutes.', null),
  ('lemon-chicken-new-potatoes', 5, 'Check the chicken is cooked through, then squeeze the remaining lemon over the whole tray before serving.', null),
  ('mackerel-green-lentils', 1, 'Heat half the oil and soften the onion for 6 minutes, then add the garlic for a minute more.', null),
  ('mackerel-green-lentils', 2, 'Stir in the lentils and warm them through, then wilt the spinach into them. Season well.', null),
  ('mackerel-green-lentils', 3, 'Meanwhile get a separate pan very hot with the rest of the oil.', null),
  ('mackerel-green-lentils', 4, 'Season the mackerel and lay it in skin side down. Press it flat for the first few seconds so the skin does not curl, and cook for 3 to 4 minutes until the skin releases cleanly.', null),
  ('mackerel-green-lentils', 5, 'Flip it for a final minute.', null),
  ('mackerel-green-lentils', 6, 'Squeeze the lemon over the lentils, fold the parsley through, and sit the mackerel on top.', null),
  ('mexican-tray-bake', 1, 'Preheat the oven to 200°C/ 180°C (fan)/ gas 6, chop your potato into bite-sized pieces and then deseed your pepper and chop into bite-sized pieces.', null),
  ('mexican-tray-bake', 2, 'Cut your cherry tomatoes in half.', null),
  ('mexican-tray-bake', 3, 'Drain and rinse your black beans. Add the chopped potato to a mixing bowl with the chopped pepper, halved cherry tomatoes and drained black beans. Add your Ground smoked paprika, cumin, chilli flakes and 3 tbsp of olive oil and give everything a good mix to coat before transferring to a baking tray and seasoning with salt and pepper.', null),
  ('mexican-tray-bake', 4, 'Place in the oven for an initial 15-20 min or until the potato has softened and have a tidy up!', null),
  ('mexican-tray-bake', 5, 'Crumble your Feta into small bite-sized pieces and chop your coriander finely, including the stalks.', null),
  ('mexican-tray-bake', 6, 'After the initial 15-20 min, remove your veggies from the oven and sprinkle over the crumbled Feta. Return to the oven and cook for a further  5-10 min.', null),
  ('mexican-tray-bake', 7, 'Combine your chipotle paste with your natural yoghurt in a ramekin to create your chipotle yoghurt dressing.

Remove your baked veggies and feta from the oven, garnish with the chopped coriander and serve.', null),
  ('mini-frittata-bites', 1, 'Preheat the oven to 180C, fan assisted.', null),
  ('mini-frittata-bites', 2, 'Crack the eggs into a bowl, whisk thoroughly and season with salt and pepper.', null),
  ('mini-frittata-bites', 3, 'Finely chop your spinach and other veggies and add to the bowl along with your chopped bacon medallions.', null),
  ('mini-frittata-bites', 4, 'Spray a muffin tray with oil and evenly distribute the mixture between the 6 holes.', null),
  ('mini-frittata-bites', 5, 'Place in the centre of the oven and bake for 18 to 20 minutes, until the top is golden and the bites are firm but springy to touch.', null),
  ('mini-frittata-bites', 6, 'Enjoy warm, or pop in the fridge for up to 4 days. They freeze for up to 3 months.', null),
  ('mushroom-spinach-omelette', 1, 'Heat the oil in a non-stick pan over a medium-high heat and cook the mushrooms until they have taken some colour, about 4 minutes. Do not crowd them or they steam.', null),
  ('mushroom-spinach-omelette', 2, 'Add the spinach and let it wilt, then tip the lot onto a plate.', null),
  ('mushroom-spinach-omelette', 3, 'Beat the eggs, season, and pour into the same pan over a medium heat.', null),
  ('mushroom-spinach-omelette', 4, 'Draw the setting edges into the middle with a spatula and tilt the pan so the raw egg runs into the gaps.', null),
  ('mushroom-spinach-omelette', 5, 'When it is just set but still glossy, spoon the mushrooms and spinach over one half, scatter the cheddar, and fold it over.', null),
  ('mushroom-spinach-omelette', 6, 'Slide it onto a plate and eat while it is hot.', null),
  ('pineapple-yogurt-pot', 1, 'Spoon the yogurt into a jar or a bowl.', null),
  ('pineapple-yogurt-pot', 2, 'Stir the honey through it rather than leaving it sitting on top, so every spoonful gets some.', null),
  ('pineapple-yogurt-pot', 3, 'Add the pineapple.', null),
  ('pineapple-yogurt-pot', 4, 'Keep the granola separate until you are about to eat, or it goes soft overnight.', null),
  ('prawn-pineapple-stir-fry', 1, 'Boil a kettle. Deseed the red pepper and cut into thin strips.', null),
  ('prawn-pineapple-stir-fry', 2, 'Remove the pineapple from the can, saving the can and juice for later, and chop into quarters.', null),
  ('prawn-pineapple-stir-fry', 3, 'Heat a large, wide-based pan with a drizzle of vegetable oil over a high heat. Once hot, add the chopped pepper and pineapple quarters with a pinch of salt and cook for 4 to 5 minutes, until the pineapple has slightly caramelised.', null),
  ('prawn-pineapple-stir-fry', 4, 'Meanwhile, peel and finely slice the garlic. Slice, do not chop.', null),
  ('prawn-pineapple-stir-fry', 5, 'Add the egg noodles to a pot and cover with boiled water until fully submerged. Bring to the boil over a high heat and cook for 5 to 6 minutes, until cooked with a slight bite. Drain and set aside, reserving a cup of the starchy noodle water.', null),
  ('prawn-pineapple-stir-fry', 6, 'Lower the heat to medium-high and add the sliced garlic and chilli flakes to the pan. Cook for 1 to 2 minutes until softened. Go easy on the chilli if you would rather.', null),
  ('prawn-pineapple-stir-fry', 7, 'While the garlic softens, add the soy sauce and toasted sesame oil to the can with the reserved pineapple juice. This is your stir-fry sauce.', null),
  ('prawn-pineapple-stir-fry', 8, 'Once the garlic has softened, add the cornflour to the pan and mix everything well.', null),
  ('prawn-pineapple-stir-fry', 9, 'Add the king prawns and the stir-fry sauce and cook for 4 to 5 minutes, until the prawns are cooked through and the sauce is sticky.', null),
  ('prawn-pineapple-stir-fry', 10, 'While the prawns cook, trim and slice the spring onion on the diagonal.', null),
  ('prawn-pineapple-stir-fry', 11, 'Add the drained noodles to the pan with a splash of the reserved starchy noodle water to loosen the sauce, and stir everything together.', null),
  ('prawn-pineapple-stir-fry', 12, 'Serve with the sliced spring onion sprinkled over the top.', null),
  ('pre-run-smoothie', 1, 'Put everything in a blender.', null),
  ('pre-run-smoothie', 2, 'Blitz for a good 45 seconds. Longer than feels necessary: the oats need breaking down or it drinks gritty.', null),
  ('pre-run-smoothie', 3, 'Pour into a glass and drink about an hour before you head out.', null),
  ('protein-recovery-shake', 1, 'Put the milk in the blender first. Powder on the bottom welds itself to the blades.', null),
  ('protein-recovery-shake', 2, 'Add everything else and blitz for 30 seconds.', null),
  ('protein-recovery-shake', 3, 'Drink it within the hour after finishing.', null),
  ('race-morning-bagel', 1, 'Split and toast the bagel if you like it warm. Untoasted is fine and quicker.', null),
  ('race-morning-bagel', 2, 'Spread the peanut butter thinly over both halves. Thin matters: fat slows everything down on a race morning.', null),
  ('race-morning-bagel', 3, 'Lay the banana over the top and trickle the maple syrup on.', null),
  ('race-morning-bagel', 4, 'Eat about two to three hours before you start, with a glass of water.', null),
  ('red-lentil-vegetable-soup', 1, 'Heat the oil in a large pan and cook the onion, carrot and celery gently for 10 minutes. Do not rush this part, it is where the flavour comes from.', null),
  ('red-lentil-vegetable-soup', 2, 'Stir in the garlic and cumin for a minute.', null),
  ('red-lentil-vegetable-soup', 3, 'Add the lentils, tomatoes and stock, and bring it up to a simmer.', null),
  ('red-lentil-vegetable-soup', 4, 'Cook for 25 to 30 minutes, until the lentils have collapsed and it has thickened.', null),
  ('red-lentil-vegetable-soup', 5, 'Season properly and squeeze the lemon in at the end.', null),
  ('red-lentil-vegetable-soup', 6, 'Cool completely before freezing in portions. It keeps 5 days in the fridge and 3 months frozen.', null),
  ('salmon-sweet-potato-broccoli', 1, 'Heat the oven to 200C fan.', null),
  ('salmon-sweet-potato-broccoli', 2, 'Toss the sweet potato wedges with half the oil, the paprika and salt, and roast for 20 minutes.', null),
  ('salmon-sweet-potato-broccoli', 3, 'Rub the salmon with the remaining oil and season it.', null),
  ('salmon-sweet-potato-broccoli', 4, 'Make space on the tray, add the salmon skin side down, and roast for 10 to 12 minutes until it flakes.', null),
  ('salmon-sweet-potato-broccoli', 5, 'Steam or boil the broccoli for 4 minutes while the salmon finishes. It should still have some bite.', null),
  ('salmon-sweet-potato-broccoli', 6, 'Squeeze the lemon over everything and serve.', null),
  ('sausage-ragu', 1, 'Heat a large, wide-based pan (ideally non-stick) with a drizzle of olive oil over a high heat. Add your sausage meat to the pre-heated pan with your bay leaf and a pinch of salt, then  cook for 2-3 min or until beginning to brown, breaking it up with a wooden spoon as you go.', null),
  ('sausage-ragu', 2, 'Meanwhile, add your pasta to a pot of boiled water with a large pinch of salt and bring to the boil over a high heat. Cook for 4-6 min or until cooked with a slight bite (allow a little longer if using dried pasta). Once done, drain, reserving a cup of the starchy pasta water for your ragù.', null),
  ('sausage-ragu', 3, 'Once the sauce has thickened, add a knob of butter and half your cracked black pepper (you''ll use the rest later!) and give everything a good stir to combine.', null),
  ('sausage-ragu', 4, 'Stir your drained pasta into the sauce and give everything a gentle mix, until the pasta is coated in the sauce, discard the bay leaf and add a splash of your reserved starchy pasta water if your sauce is looking a little dry.

Serve topped with grated parmesan and remaining cracked black pepper.', null),
  ('smoked-salmon-scrambled-eggs', 1, 'Whisk the eggs with the milk and a good grind of pepper. Do not season with salt yet, the salmon brings plenty.', null),
  ('smoked-salmon-scrambled-eggs', 2, 'Melt the butter in a cold pan over a low heat, then add the eggs.', null),
  ('smoked-salmon-scrambled-eggs', 3, 'Stir slowly and constantly. Low and slow is the whole trick: pull the pan off the heat while they still look slightly underdone, because they carry on cooking.', null),
  ('smoked-salmon-scrambled-eggs', 4, 'Toast the sourdough and tear the smoked salmon over it.', null),
  ('smoked-salmon-scrambled-eggs', 5, 'Spoon the eggs on top, scatter with parsley and eat immediately.', null),
  ('sweet-potato-black-bean-chilli', 1, 'Heat the oil and cook the onion and pepper for 7 minutes until soft.', null),
  ('sweet-potato-black-bean-chilli', 2, 'Add the garlic, cumin and paprika for a minute.', null),
  ('sweet-potato-black-bean-chilli', 3, 'Stir in the sweet potato, beans, tomatoes and stock.', null),
  ('sweet-potato-black-bean-chilli', 4, 'Simmer for 25 to 30 minutes, until the sweet potato is tender but still holding its shape. Stir now and then so it does not catch.', null),
  ('sweet-potato-black-bean-chilli', 5, 'Season, and scatter the coriander over just before serving.', null),
  ('sweet-potato-black-bean-chilli', 6, 'Cool completely before freezing. Fridge 4 days, freezer 3 months.', null),
  ('tofu-edamame-noodles', 1, 'Soak or boil the noodles to the packet timing, then drain and rinse them in cold water so they do not clag together.', null),
  ('tofu-edamame-noodles', 2, 'Get a wide pan properly hot with the oil, then fry the tofu without moving it for 3 minutes so it forms a crust. Turn and repeat.', null),
  ('tofu-edamame-noodles', 3, 'Add the pepper, ginger and garlic and stir fry for 2 minutes.', null),
  ('tofu-edamame-noodles', 4, 'Add the edamame and the soy sauce and toss for another minute.', null),
  ('tofu-edamame-noodles', 5, 'Fold the noodles through until everything is coated and hot.', null),
  ('tofu-edamame-noodles', 6, 'Finish with the spring onion and the toasted sesame seeds.', null),
  ('tuna-pasta-with-passata', 1, 'Cook the pasta in well salted water, and keep a mugful of the water before you drain it.', null),
  ('tuna-pasta-with-passata', 2, 'Meanwhile heat the oil and soften the onion for 5 minutes, then add the garlic for one more.', null),
  ('tuna-pasta-with-passata', 3, 'Pour in the passata, season, and let it bubble while the pasta finishes.', null),
  ('tuna-pasta-with-passata', 4, 'Flake in the drained tuna and warm it through gently. Stirring it hard turns it to paste.', null),
  ('tuna-pasta-with-passata', 5, 'Drain the pasta and add it to the sauce with a splash of the reserved water, tossing until it clings.', null),
  ('tuna-pasta-with-passata', 6, 'Serve with the parmesan and the basil over the top.', null),
  ('turkey-vegetable-chilli', 1, 'Heat the oil in a large pan and brown the turkey mince in two batches. One batch steams and goes grey.', null),
  ('turkey-vegetable-chilli', 2, 'Add the onion and pepper and cook for 6 to 7 minutes.', null),
  ('turkey-vegetable-chilli', 3, 'Stir in the garlic, cumin, paprika and chilli and cook for a minute until fragrant.', null),
  ('turkey-vegetable-chilli', 4, 'Add the tomatoes, beans and sweetcorn, season well, and simmer gently for 25 minutes.', null),
  ('turkey-vegetable-chilli', 5, 'Taste and adjust the salt and chilli at the end, not the beginning.', null),
  ('turkey-vegetable-chilli', 6, 'Cool fully before portioning. Fridge 4 days, freezer 3 months.', null);

